  "title": "Entropy and large deviations for Latin squares",
  "abstract": "A large deviation principle for uniform labeled Latin squares in the full ordered Latinon cut distance, at speed n squared with extended relative entropy as a good rate function. The space retains both row and column orders. For every finite family of strict order patterns and every finite-rate target, the development gives bilateral local logarithmic counts with binomial finite normalization and second-order constant -2. Neighborhood radii may depend on the target and are chosen before the order threshold. Empty compatible fibers have eventually empty finite neighborhoods. The proof includes a uniform lower counting theorem for bounded positive tristochastic profiles and a transportation correction with exact support, bounded entries and l1 cost at most 5/2 times the total margin defect. The entropy convention is Ent = -KL.",
